+# ADR Audit — 2026-08-16
+
+Status: Completed
+Repository: `KdGithubIt/GameEngine`
+Baseline: `e99d227ab40a7d839afa718e40ab372ec1899f32`
+
+## Scope
+
+This audit separates two questions that had become mixed together after the ADR
+sequence passed 100 records:
+
+1. **Registry integrity:** Does every ADR exist, have a usable status, and appear
+   in the chronological index with supersession represented correctly?
+2. **Current-contract alignment:** Do the recent/cross-cutting ADRs, canonical
+   specification, workspace structure, and representative implementation
+   surfaces still describe the same architecture?
+
+Registry integrity was checked across every numbered ADR file in the baseline.
+Implementation alignment was intentionally risk-based rather than a claim that
+every line of every historical ADR was re-proven against code.
+
+## Registry result
+
+The baseline contains 129 ADR files but only 127 distinct ADR numbers. Two
+concurrent decision streams reused ADR 0122, and a later renderer change also
+reused ADR 0123. This audit keeps the first-merged Proposed sequence as ADR
+0122–0126 and the already-merged Native 2D proposal as ADR 0127. The later
+Accepted renderer-owned full-IBL record moves from ADR 0122 to ADR 0128, and the
+later Accepted generic directional/point/spot-lighting record moves from ADR
+0123 to ADR 0129.
+
+After that correction:
+
+- 119 records are Accepted.
+- 4 records are Superseded.
+- 6 records are Proposed.
+- No Rejected ADR file is present.
+
+The Superseded records are:
+
+| ADR | Replaced by |
+| --- | --- |
+| 0019 | ADR 0022 |
+| 0093 | ADR 0095 |
+| 0108 | ADR 0112 |
+| 0109 | ADR 0112 |
+
+The Proposed records are:
+
+| ADR | Proposal area |
+| --- | --- |
+| 0122 | Spatial audio mixer and authoring UX |
+| 0123 | Stateful Behavior Tree execution and debugging |
+| 0124 | Production navigation mesh and bake workflow |
+| 0125 | VFX effect authoring and runtime architecture |
+| 0126 | Timeline / Sequencer authoring and runtime |
+| 0127 | Native 2D gameplay and authoring architecture |
+
+These six proposals are deliberately excluded from the current-decision map and
+from implementation-conformance claims in this audit.
+
+### Concurrent ADR-number collisions
+
+The Proposed 0122–0126 bundle reached `main` before the renderer full-IBL change.
+The later renderer merge introduced another ADR 0122. A subsequent Accepted
+generic-lighting merge introduced ADR 0123 while the Proposed Behavior Tree
+record already owned that number. Native 2D then reached `main` as Proposed ADR
+0127 before this conflict repair was finalized.
+
+Renumbering only the later Accepted renderer records to ADR 0128 and ADR 0129 is
+the smallest collision-free repair. It leaves the first-merged Proposed sequence,
+its cross-references, and the already-merged Native 2D identity intact. The
+renderer decisions, statuses, public/runtime contracts, and implementations do
+not change; only their ADR identities and references are repaired.
+
+The previous `docs/adr/README.md` was not a faithful registry:
+
+- it omitted ADRs 0093, 0094, 0095, 0102, 0105, and the Proposed ADRs 0122
+  through 0127;
+- it contained duplicate ADR 0122 and ADR 0123 identities while showing only
+  the later renderer records in the README;
+- it placed 0019, 0108, and 0109 under a heading named `Accepted Decisions`;
+- it contained a one-off ADR 0052 link above the index; and
+- it retained a `Phase 41+ ADR Targets` table that duplicated a small historical
+  slice after the repository had progressed to ADR 0129.
+
+The reorganized index distinguishes the current decision map from the full
+chronological history, includes all previously missing records, keeps Proposed
+records visibly separate from the current contract, and makes every ADR number
+unique through ADR 0129.
+
+## Current-contract alignment
+
+### ADR-number repair
+
+Renderer-owned full IBL is now ADR 0128. Generic directional, point, and spot
+direct lighting is now ADR 0129. Both decisions remain Accepted. The code merged
+with those records already implements their renderer behavior, so this is an
+identifier repair rather than an architecture reversal.
+
+### Runtime decomposition
+
+ADR 0113's package set is present in the workspace: `core`, `assets`, `rig`,
+`physics`, `animation`, `gameplay`, `render-runtime`, `platform`, `import`,
+`scripting`, and `scene` exist alongside `renderer`, `engine`, `ecs`, and
+`authoring`.
+
+The audit does **not** interpret that as "every old `engine` file must be gone".
+The `engine` package still contains compatibility facade modules and concrete
+cross-domain composition, which ADR 0113 explicitly allows when moving the code
+downward would introduce the wrong dependency direction or a cycle.
+
+One real documentation drift was found inside ADR 0113 itself: its CI section
+still described per-crate changed-path mapping and referred to full validation
+on `master`. The current workflow derives package ownership from Cargo metadata,
+forbids a duplicated package/path table, and uses `main`. The operational text
+is updated without changing the runtime architecture decision.
+
+### Canonical authoring specification
+
+`docs/AI_FRIENDLY_AUTHORING_SPEC.md` had accumulated current-contract drift:
+
+- Section 6 still presented the pre-0113 `graph`/`graph_bt` future workspace
+  sketch instead of the current runtime-domain package structure.
+- Section 7.2 still required compatibility loading for entities missing fields
+  that ADR 0115 makes mandatory in the current format.
+- Section 15 still described migration as part of the normal save pipeline even
+  though ADR 0115 establishes current-format-only loading.
+- Historical Phase 2.5 text referred to a nonexistent `Open Decision #7`.
+- Section 23 still summarized ADR 0099 as retaining the legacy singular
+  VMD/old-ID compatibility path that ADR 0115 removes.
+- The single-version table still listed material schema version 2 even though
+  ADR 0120 and the current authoring code use material schema version 3.
+- The same table treated `project.json` as version 1 even though the current
+  project identity contract is schema version 2 with `ProjectId` and
+  `engine_version`.
+- The newly merged local-light authoring contract referred to the colliding ADR
+  0123 identity instead of the repaired ADR 0129 identity.
+
+Those contradictions are corrected. Historical phase descriptions remain in the
+specification, but they are explicitly subordinate to later Accepted ADRs and
+current normative sections.
+
+### Representative implementation checks
+
+The following current surfaces were sampled because they exercise recent
+cross-cutting decisions:
+
+- ADR 0116: animation event installation is present through the animation
+  runtime and scene-spawn integration rather than a separate component-level
+  authoring event contract.
+- ADR 0117: `ProjectId`, project schema version 2, and
+  `engine-project-lifecycle` are present.
+- ADRs 0118–0120: material schema version 3 and the generic
+  metallic/roughness, occlusion, normal-scale, and occlusion-strength fields
+  are present across authoring/runtime/import boundaries.
+- ADR 0121: Editor MCP transport and shared Scene/Asset MCP/CLI authoring slices
+  are present in the baseline.
+- ADRs 0122–0127 are Proposed and were status/index audited only. Their decisions
+  are not treated as current implementation requirements and were not scored as
+  implementation drift.
+- ADR 0128 is Accepted and its renderer-owned full-IBL implementation is present
+  in the render-runtime changes that introduced the decision.
+- ADR 0129 is Accepted and the baseline contains the stable
+  `engine.point_light` / `engine.spot_light` authoring IDs, 16/8 local-light
+  budgets, deterministic selection, and shared StandardLit direct-light path
+  introduced with that decision.
+
+These checks support the conclusion that the recent architecture is broadly
+tracking implementation. They do not certify every historical phase-specific
+statement as current.
+
+## What was deliberately not changed
+
+- Historical ADR numbers and file names were not renumbered except for the two
+  later colliding Accepted renderer records, which moved to 0128 and 0129
+  without changing their decisions or statuses.
+- Accepted ADRs were not marked Superseded merely because their implementation
+  details are old; a later decision must actually replace the decision.
+- Historical metadata formatting (`Status:` versus `- Status:` and title
+  punctuation) was not normalized across the full registry, because that would
+  create large review noise without changing the contract.
+- No serialized schema, Stable ID, public Rust API, crate dependency, or runtime
+  behavior changed in this audit.
+- No `.github/**` or Dispatcher trust-boundary file changed.
+
+## Follow-up
+
+A lightweight ADR-registry checker would be useful to prevent future duplicate
+numeric prefixes, index omissions, and invalid status values. That should be
+implemented separately if it is made a CI requirement, because CI/build
+infrastructure has a different validation and trust-boundary impact from this
+documentation cleanup.
+
+A second future cleanup may move long completed phase narratives out of the
+canonical authoring specification into historical phase documentation. This
+audit only corrected statements that could mislead a contributor about the
+current contract.
